        "worked_solution": "To find $\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202x\u2202y}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202y}$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\u2202}^{2}f}{\u2202x\u2202y} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\frac{\u2202f}{\u2202y}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\frac{{e}^{y}}{x+y}) \\\\  & ={e}^{y}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{(x+y)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{y}}{(x+y)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
